+# AutoCraft in the folder intranet
+
+This installation contains the production dashboard and Node/SQLite service from Storytold AutoCraft commit `0bcc1f8d681609233d2f6f0d1f4e359e994079e0`. The folder launcher binds the dashboard to `127.0.0.1:8993` and uses GitHub sign-in. The current Windows user, SYSTEM and Administrators are the only principals allowed in the protected default `.private` directory.
+
+1. Register or reuse an approved GitHub OAuth app with callback `http://127.0.0.1:8993/auth/callback`. See [GitHub's loopback callback documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/apps/oauth-apps/building-oauth-apps/authorizing-oauth-apps#loopback-redirect-urls).
+2. Run `Configure AutoCraft.cmd` and enter the OAuth client ID and secret in that local window. It creates the secrets file once and generates the session key. Keep `.private` outside source control and backups accessible to other users.
+3. Set the first operator from a terminal with `"AutoCraft CLI.cmd" access add YOUR-GITHUB-LOGIN --operator`.
+4. Run `Start AutoCraft.cmd` and open [AutoCraft](http://127.0.0.1:8993/).
+
+`AutoCraft CLI.cmd` uses `.private/mirror.db` by default. Keep the database and session key together when backing up this installation. The upstream runner's provider-backed tools require a supported isolated Linux runtime with bubblewrap and configured model and repository credentials. See the bundled [operations guide](docs/operations.md).
